ost lane (experimental, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md)\nbb.edn:16:  bootstrap:jolt\nbb.edn:17:  {:doc \"Materialize the jolt-toolchain.edn pins into build/tools/jolt (mise Chez/CMake checked, jolt cloned at the full SHA, never pulled) and write build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"\nbb.edn:19:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:21:  test:jolt-bootstrap-neg\nbb.edn:22:  {:doc \"Copy/revert the jolt clone under gitignored build/bootstrap-neg (deleted on success, retained on failure) and declare a synthetic patch and prove bootstrap refuses it unapplied or corrupted, then accepts it applied (JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR selects the source clone)\"\nbb.edn:24:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\" \"--test-negative\")))}\nbb.edn:26:  smoke:jolt\nbb.edn:27:  {:doc \"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:30:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:32:  jolt\nbb.edn:33:  {:doc \"Run jolt -Srepro -M:jolt with the arguments given (a script path, -e ...), under build/tools/jolt-env.sh\"\nbb.edn:36:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt \\\"$@\\\"\"\nbb.edn:37:                         \"jolt\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:39:  qualify:jolt-libcrypto\nbb.edn:40:  {:doc \"J1b requalification: print this platform's observed libcrypto identity {:canonical-path :version-num :version :sha256} for jolt-toolchain.edn :native :libcrypto :qualified (the digest from bb and from the library, required equal); changes nothing (needs a built wrapper: bb build:jolt-native, or --requalify after a library change)\"\nbb.edn:42:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:44:  probe:jolt-crypto\nbb.edn:45:  {:doc \"J1b: libcrypto provenance (qualified, missing, undeclared, version-floor, wrong-library-first, Linux LD_PRELOAD) and 256 MiB :blocking hash collect-safety, each in a child jolt process (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:47:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-crypto/probes/run.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:49:  test:jolt-j5\nbb.edn:50:  {:doc \"J5 acceptance: one Python session through the JVM and jolt REPL entry points with the standard catalog (output equal line for line), the multiline probe sequence, and the unavailable-library REPL legs (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:52:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j5_acceptance.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:54:  probe:jolt-j5\nbb.edn:55:  {:doc \"J5b: the native Python parser's budget (input 4 MiB; in-parser guards: 8192 rule frames, 4096 SLL lookahead links, 256 full-LL links, on a 16 MiB parse thread): the review's repros, at/over per shape against the predicted table, 10x the old crash depths, the JVM's packets (incl. a 20,000-deep 1+ tree), the old crash depths in children on the jolt thread, injected C++ faults, the abort-is-a-failure property, lifecycle and unavailable-library legs. Args select legs: budget below crash inject abort unavailable (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:57:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j5_run.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:59:  calibrate:jolt-j5\nbb.edn:60:  {:doc \"J5b C4 + J5c: build the guards-off calibration variant of native/jolt-parser and record each nesting shape's stack cost per rule frame and per lookahead link on the 16 MiB parse thread (asserting every bound fits a quarter of the stack; writes build/j5b/calibration.edn), or, with --work, the work metric's per-shape counts and the corpus sweep the work bound derives from (writes build/j5b/work.edn; needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:63:                         \"src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:65:  probe:jolt-file\nbb.edn:66:  {:doc \"J4a: native/jolt-file gates, each in a child process: JVM-identical frame bytes (both hash algorithms), F2 s32BE prefixes, strict reads, injected short/EINTR/zero-progress/error transfers, corrupt-open byte identity, idempotent close, no fd or native-memory leak, a full collection during a 1 GiB :blocking pwrite, missing/wrong-layout wrapper refused before guest work, exported-symbol allowlist (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:68:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:70:  probe:jolt-udp\nbb.edn:71:  {:doc \"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:73:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\")))}\nbb.edn:75:  probe:jolt-tcp\nbb.edn:76:  {:doc \"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:81:                               (println \"== probe:jolt-tcp section\" s)\nbb.edn:83:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\nbb.edn:84:                                                \"jolt\" s))])\nbb.edn:86:           (println \"probe:jolt-tcp exits\" (pr-str results))\nbb.edn:89:  probe:jolt-ws\nbb.edn:90:  {:doc \"J6e: the jolt WebSocket host adapter (dao.stream.ws.jolt, the yin.repl.host shadow, the jolt -main wiring), one child jolt process per section: closure (C1), handshake (C2), bind (C3), address (C4), io (C5), close (C6), shutdown (C7, the real owner loop), isolation (C8), driver (C9, deadline folding, a --headless --port child), fairness (C10); native memory and registries empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:95:                               (println \"== probe:jolt-ws section\" s)\nbb.edn:97:                                                \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj \\\"$1\\\"\"\nbb.edn:98:                                                \"jolt\" s))])\nbb.edn:100:           (println \"probe:jolt-ws exits\" (pr-str results))\nbb.edn:103:   workload-w:jolt\nbb.edn:104:   {:doc \"J6g: pre-registered Workload W, with an independent five-minute watchdog and ten-second sampler; one jolt worker serves two peers while stepping the REPL (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\"\nbb.edn:107:                          \"exec bb src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj \\\"$@\\\"\"\nbb.edn:108:                         \"jolt\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:110:  build:jolt-native\nbb.edn:111:  {:doc \"Fetch (by pinned SHA-256, only when absent) and build the jolt-toolchain.edn :native sources with the mise-pinned CMake into build/native/<platform>/\"\nbb.edn:113:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_native.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:115:  test:jolt-host\nbb.edn:116:  {:doc \"J1: the dao.host oracle (conformance, bytes, float, text tests) under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj; counts per namespace, nonzero exit on any failure, error or load failure (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:119:                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.host.conformance-test dao.host.bytes-test dao.host.float-test dao.host.text-test\")))}\nbb.edn:124:  ;; build/j2-logs/; every step is its own jolt process.\nbb.edn:125:  probe:jolt-j2\nbb.edn:126:  {:doc \"J2: staged load probe of the J2 load order under -M:jolt:jolt-test, one namespace per process (load-ok / first failing require / first unresolved symbol / first load-time error + the loaded-libs delta asserting dao.stream.transit absent); logs under build/j2-logs/probe (src/dev/jolt_j2_probe.clj; needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\nbb.edn:128:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"probe\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:138:  demo:jolt\nbb.edn:139:  {:doc \"J3: tracked yin.demo on JVM and jolt; require SUCCESS: sum(0..100) = 5050\"\nbb.edn:141:                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj\" \"--demo\")))}\nbb.edn:143:  test:jolt-shell\nbb.edn:144:  {:doc \"J3: one deadline-bounded transcript corpus on JVM and jolt, held stdin, exact output/exit checks and startup timings\"\nbb.edn:146:                                    \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:148:  test:jolt-core\nbb.edn:149:  {:doc \"J2: every applicable pure suite (test/dao/host, jing, data, space, portable stream, yin/vm) under jolt, one namespace per process through src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj, fast and ^:slow alike (Q3), nonzero exit on any failure; excluded suites are printed and recorded with reason/capability/owner\"\nbb.edn:151:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"core\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:153:  test:jolt-core:diag\nbb.edn:154:  {:doc \"J2 DIAGNOSTIC: test:jolt-core with the :jolt-diag alias added (the J1 corpus-loader stand-in for dao.jing.cbor-fixtures)\"\nbb.edn:156:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"core\" \"--diag\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:158:  test:jolt-j2-jvm\nbb.edn:159:  {:doc \"J2: the JVM counts baseline — the same included namespaces on the JVM, one process, clojure.test run-tests per namespace (src/dev/jolt_j2_jvm_runner.clj), per-namespace counts to build/j2-logs/jvm-summary.edn for the jolt-vs-JVM diff\"\nbb.edn:161:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"jvm\" *command-line-args*)))}\nbb.edn:163:  test:jolt-j2-manifest\nbb.edn:164:  {:doc \"J2: self-test the applicability manifest guard with a temporary test tree; no jolt or natives needed\"\nbb.edn:166:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_manifest_check.clj\")))}\nbb.edn:168:  report:jolt-j2\nbb.edn:169:  {:doc \"J2: the jolt-vs-JVM per-namespace count table from build/j2-logs/{core,jvm}-summary.edn; runs nothing\"\nbb.edn:171:           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj\" \"report\")))}\nbb.edn:173:  test:jolt-carrier\nbb.edn:174:  {:doc \"J2: the cross-host integer-carrier test (Q1: carriers named by value). `encode` runs the JVM side (java -cp over the test:dev classpath, writes build/j2-logs/carrier-fixtures.edn); `verify` runs the jolt side (decode both rows, assert equal bytes and equal results)\"\nbb.edn:179:                                      \"mkdir -p build/j2-logs && java -cp \\\"$(clojure -Spath -A:test -A:dev)\\\" clojure.main src/dev/jolt_carrier_test.clj --encode\"))\nbb.edn:181:                                      \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_carrier_test.clj --verify\"))\nbb.edn:184:  test:jolt-cbor-override\nbb.edn:187:           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true :shutdown nil} \"bb\" \"src/dev/jolt_cbor_override_check.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n/home/sto/.local/bin/mise\n/usr/local/bin/clojure\nls: cannot access 'build': No such file or directory\nls: cannot access 'target': No such file or directory\nls: cannot access '/home/sto/.cache/datom-jolt': No such file or directory\nls: cannot access '/home/sto/.local/bin/jolt': No such file or directory\nrc=0\ncollab/jolt/1794773141000-architect-j7-udp-dht.prompt.md\ncollab/jolt/1794773141000-engineer-j7-udp-dht.prompt.md\ncollab/jolt/j7-review-prompt.md\nLinux jupiter.stigmergy.systems 7.0.0-38-generic #38~24.04.4-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon Sep 14 16:37:11 UTC 2 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj && sed -n '1,115p' deps.edn && rg -n -A10 -B3 '\"'^  run-clj'\"' bb.edn && git diff --check origin/master..HEAD && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj && sed -n '1,115p' deps.edn && rg -n -A10 -B3 '\"'^  run-clj'\"' bb.edn && git diff --check origin/master..HEAD && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"(ns jolt-bootstrap\n  \"bb bootstrap:jolt — materialize the jolt toolchain declared in\n   jolt-toolchain.edn (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.3, §6.1).\n\n   * Chez and CMake come from mise at the exact pinned versions; this task\n     checks them and never installs or upgrades them (`mise install` does).\n   * jolt is cloned from the declared origin into build/tools/jolt and checked\n     out at the declared full SHA with its recursive submodules. An existing\n     checkout is verified, never pulled: a HEAD, submodule or dirty-tree\n     mismatch fails the task. Declared patches and re-minted seeds are accepted\n     only at their recorded digests and after behavioural smoke tests.\n     The one-time nil-platform acceptance is remembered in\n     build/tools/jolt-patches.edn; deleting that record resets it.\n     Advancing the pin is the upgrade gate's job.\n   * build/tools/jolt-env.sh is written with JOLT_CHEZ set explicitly, so jolt\n     never searches PATH for a Chez.\n   * First of all, on a Debian-family host, the :os-packages :debian\n     :required packages are checked with dpkg-query; a missing one fails the\n     task before mise is asked for anything, naming the exact\n     `sudo apt-get install -y ...` command. Nothing here runs sudo or apt.\n     Test seam: JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DEBIAN_INSTALLED=pkg,pkg,... treats the\n     host as Debian and those packages as the installed set (no dpkg-query).\n\n   Exit status is nonzero on any mismatch.\"\n  (:require [clojure.java.io]\n            [babashka.fs :as fs]\n            [babashka.process :as p]\n            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.set :as set]\n            [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(defn- fail!\n  [& msg]\n  (binding [*out* *err*]\n    (println \"bootstrap:jolt FAILED:\" (apply str msg)))\n  (System/exit 1))\n\n\n(defn- sh\n  \"Run a command, answer trimmed stdout; fail the task on a nonzero exit.\"\n  [& args]\n  (let [opts (if (map? (first args)) (first args) {})\n        cmd (if (map? (first args)) (rest args) args)\n        r (apply p/shell (merge {:out :string :err :string :continue true} opts) cmd)]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n      (fail! (str/join \" \" cmd) \" exited \" (:exit r) \"\\n\" (:err r)\n             \"\\nRemedy: git -C build/tools/jolt checkout -- . && bb bootstrap:jolt\"))\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\n\n\n(defn- mise-bin\n  \"The path of executable `exe` from mise tool `tool` at exactly `version`\n   (mise's own resolution: the layout differs per platform).\"\n  [tool version exe]\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                   \"mise\" \"exec\" (str tool \"@\" version) \"--\" \"which\" exe)]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r))\n      (fail! \"mise has no \" tool \"@\" version \" installed; run `mise install \" tool \"`\"))\n    (str/trim (:out r))))\n\n\n(defn- check-chez\n  [{:keys [version binary threaded]}]\n  (let [scheme (mise-bin \"chezscheme\" version (str (fs/file-name binary)))\n        v (sh scheme \"--version\")\n        t (sh {:in \"(display (threaded?))\"} scheme \"-q\")]\n    (when-not (= version v) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (when (and threaded (not= \"#t\" t)) (fail! \"Chez at \" scheme \" is not threaded\"))\n    (println \"chez\" v \"threaded\" t scheme)\n    scheme))\n\n\n(defn- check-cmake\n  [{:keys [version]}]\n  (let [cmake (mise-bin \"cmake\" version \"cmake\")\n        v (first (str/split-lines (sh cmake \"--version\")))]\n    (when-not (= (str \"cmake version \" version) v)\n      (fail! \"CMake at \" cmake \" reports \" v \", pinned \" version))\n    (println v cmake)\n    cmake))\n\n\n(defn- submodule-shas\n  [dir]\n  ;; Not through `sh`: its trim would eat the status column of the first line\n  ;; (\" \" checked out at the recorded commit, \"-\" uninitialized, \"+\" differs).\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true}\n                   \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"status\" \"--recursive\")]\n    (when-not (zero? (:exit r)) (fail! \"git submodule status: \" (:err r)))\n    (into {}\n          (map (fn [line]\n                 (let [[sha path] (str/split (str/trim (subs line 1)) #\"\\s+\")]\n                   (when (not= \\space (first line))\n                     (fail! \"submodule \" path \" is not checked out at its recorded commit: \" line))\n                   [path sha])))\n          (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (:out r))))))\n\n\n(defn- materialize!\n  [{:keys [origin sha dir]}]\n  (when-not (fs/exists? dir)\n    (fs/create-dirs (fs/parent dir))\n    (println \"cloning\" origin \"into\" dir)\n    (sh \"git\" \"clone\" \"--no-checkout\" origin dir)\n    (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"checkout\" \"--detach\" sha)\n    (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"submodule\" \"update\" \"--init\" \"--recursive\")))\n\n\n(defn- verify!\n  [{:keys [origin sha dir submodules]}]\n  (let [head (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"rev-parse\" \"HEAD\")\n        remote (sh \"git\" \"-C\" dir \"remote\" \"get-url\" \"origin\")\n        remedy (str \"\\nRemedy: git -C build/tools/jolt checkout -- .\"\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt remote set-url origin \" origin\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt fetch origin \" sha\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt checkout --detach \" sha\n                    \" && git -C build/tools/jolt submodule update --init --recursive\"\n                    \" && bb bootstrap:jolt\"\n                    \"\\nAlternatively: rm -rf build/tools/jolt && bb bootstrap:jolt\"\n                    \"\\nPin changes go through qualify:jolt-upgrade.\")]\n    (when-not (= origin remote)\n      (fail! dir \" has origin \" remote \", declared \" origin remedy))\n    (when-not (= sha head)\n      (fail! dir \" is at \" head \", declared \" sha remedy))\n    (let [actual (submodule-shas dir)]\n      (when-not (= submodules actual)\n        (fail! \"submodule SHAs differ from jolt-toolchain.edn: \" (pr-str actual))))\n    (println \"jolt\" head \"with\" (count submodules) \"submodules verified\")))\n\n\n(defn- patch-fail!\n  [& msg]\n  (apply fail! (concat msg [\"\\nRemedy: git -C build/tools/jolt checkout -- . && bb bootstrap:jolt\"])))\n\n\n(defn- sha256\n  [path]\n  (when (fs/regular-file? path)\n    (let [digest (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \"SHA-256\")]\n      (with-open [in (clojure.java.io/input-stream (str path))]\n        (let [buf (byte-array 65536)]\n          (loop []\n            (let [n (.read in buf)]\n              (when (pos? n) (.update digest buf 0 n) (recur))))))\n      (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and 255 %)) (.digest digest))))))\n\n\n(defn- platform\n  []\n  (case [(System/getProperty \"os.name\") (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n    [\"Mac OS X\" \"aarch64\"] :darwin-arm64\n    [\"Linux\" \"amd64\"] :linux-x86_64\n    (patch-fail! \"unsupported patch platform\")))\n\n\n(defn- check-digests!\n  [dir files phase]\n  (doseq [[path hashes] files]\n    (when-not (= (phase hashes) (sha256 (fs/path dir path)))\n      (patch-fail! path \" sha256 mismatch (\" (name phase) \")\"))))\n\n\n(defn- smoke!\n  [dir scheme form expect message]\n  (let [r (p/shell {:out :string :err :string :continue true\n                    :extra-env {\"JOLT_CHEZ\" scheme \"JOLT_HOME\" dir}}\n                   (str (fs/path dir \"bin\" \"jolt\")) \"-e\" form)]\n    (when-not (and (zero? (:exit r)) (= expect (str/trim (:out r))))\n      (patch-fail! message \": \" (pr-str (:out r)) \" \" (:err r)))\n    (println \"jolt smoke\" form \"=>\" expect)))\n\n\n(defn- apply-patches!\n  [{:keys [sha dir patches]} scheme]\n  (let [plat (platform)\n        record-file (str (fs/path (fs/parent dir) \"jolt-patches.edn\"))\n        prior (when (fs/exists? record-file) (edn/read-string (slurp record-file)))\n        ;; -z preserves the status column, spaces and rename paths. Renames\n        ;; cannot be a declared patch state and fail below as unknown paths.\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\" \"build/antlr/php/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.shell.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n           ;; needs one.\n           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n                  :replace-deps {}}\n           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.shell.main\"]}\n           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
