n-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n     5\t# Task: J7 implement round — the UDP + DHT composition on jolt\n     6\tRole: engineer\n     7\tImplementers:\n     8\t- Model: gemini-3.8-flash | Assigned: 2026-11-16 03:05 +0700 | Status: active | Rationale: implements per the architect's design\n     9\t\n    10\tFIRST read collab/jolt/*architect-j7-design.findings.md in this worktree (codex's committed design) and implement its slice 1 (and slice 2 if slice 1 is green). Follow the design's order and contracts exactly; where you must deviate, record why in collab/jolt/<ts>-engineer-j7-impl.findings.md.\n    11\t\n    12\tAcceptance per slice (run locally in this worktree; mise env first):\n    13\t- bb bootstrap:jolt; build if the design requires native work.\n    14\t- jolt -Srepro -M:jolt (PATH via build/tools/jolt-env.sh) loads every new namespace.\n    15\t- The J0b regression legs the design lists pass on jolt.\n    16\t- The smoke: `echo '(+ 1 2)' | jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-yin-repl --index-store dht:/tmp/j7-smoke` boots solo (no --dht-peer) and evaluates the form; the refusal message at yin/shell/dht.cljc:255 is GONE for the composed path.\n    17\t- JVM lane unchanged: `bb run-clj` equivalent loads yin.shell.dht and yin.repl.\n    18\tCommit on this branch (fix/j7-udp-dht) per slice with evidence in the message.\n### 8.4 J7 integration\n\nJ7 integrates the probed transport through the datagram host seam:\nbound/send-failed/closed events, the maximum-datagram policy, IPv4/IPv6 and the\nhost-composed deposit medium. No reliability or queue is added beneath it. The\ndatagram-contract and DHT/linker composition are the main effort:\ndatagram/address/size/lifecycle suites, jolt legs in the DHT process and\nsigned-head tests, bind/send failures and shutdown. P2P/DHT is outside the local\nmilestone and is a parity gate, not a hidden skip.\n\n## 9. Native WebSocket\n\n### 9.1 Decisions\n\nOwner Q6: \"native websocket, no sidecar\". Owner on W2: \"CBOR-only websocket, no\nTransit port\": the jolt WebSocket composes only the `dao.stream.cbor` binary\nsubprotocol. No helper process is a supported deployment. `dao.stream.ws` keeps\nall public semantics, outcomes, bounds, custody and lifecycle; the jolt host\nadapter owns only the socket, the HTTP upgrade and RFC 6455 framing. The earlier\nrecommendation to permit a JVM sidecar is decision history only.\n\n### 9.2 The host contract (W1)\n\nV: `dao.stream.ws` knows no WebSocket library; a host adapter supplies small\nsynchronous functions and socket callbacks enter only through an adapter map\n(`src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:1-15`). A jolt build supplies the whole host\ncontract, not only the per-connection map:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
